{"name":"Blue Shutters","hex":"#93bde7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"},{"term":"shutters","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of shutter"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/shutters"}],"entries":[{"title":"Window shutter","blocks":[{"text":"A window shutter is a solid and stable window covering, usually consisting of a frame of vertical stiles and horizontal rails. Set within this frame can be louvers, solid panels, fabric, glass and almost any other item that can be mounted within a frame.\nShutters may be employed for a variety of reasons, including controlling the amount of sunlight that enters a room, to provide privacy, security, to protect against weather or unwanted intrusion or damage and to enhance the aesthetics of a building."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a6/Interior-Shutters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Window_shutter"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains blue eyes. Distant objects appear more blue because of another optical effect called aerial perspective."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg/330px-Earth-in-true-color-himawari-09.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Window_shutters.png/500px-Window_shutters.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Window_shutters.png/500px-Window_shutters.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Modern interior wooden window shutters","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWindow_shutters.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Workers_installing_shutters.jpg/500px-Workers_installing_shutters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Workers_installing_shutters.jpg/1280px-Workers_installing_shutters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Workers_installing_shutters.jpg/500px-Workers_installing_shutters.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Workers installing plantation-style shutters in a home.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWorkers_installing_shutters.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Shutters_on_a_building_in_Aix_France.jpg/500px-Shutters_on_a_building_in_Aix_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Shutters_on_a_building_in_Aix_France.jpg/1280px-Shutters_on_a_building_in_Aix_France.jpg?ut